                <pb facs="0259" n="993" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg993"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 69.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mariscal to Mr.
                            Ransom.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-18"><hi rendition="#italic">September 18,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: In compliance with Article II of
                    the convention had on the 1st of April of the current year, between the
                    representatives of the Governments of Mexico and Guatemala, at my proposal your
                    excellency has been designated to act in the arbitration provided for in said
                    article.</p>
                <p>I hope that your excellency will be pleased to accept said appointment as a token
                    of friendly deference toward both Governments; and it gratifies me to reiterate
                    the assurance of my highest regard.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Igno. Mariscal.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
